vdr-skin-anthra-common
======================

Common files for the anthra skins of the VDR text2skin plugin, packaged
for Debian.

The anthra skins by Tomas Saxer are generated from XML parts according to
a set of options. vdr-skin-anthra-update builds a skin from

  /usr/share/vdr-skin-anthra/SKIN   the skin sources (read-only)
  /etc/vdr/anthra/SKIN.conf         the options (conffile)

into /var/lib/vdr/plugins/text2skin/SKIN, the directory where text2skin
looks for its skins. Local options survive upgrades. While building, all
windows get bpp 32 (true colour, text2skin falls back to 256 colours
without a true colour OSD) and the anthra_1920_* skins get screenBase
abs1920x1080, so text2skin scales them to the real OSD size.

The skin packages (vdr-skin-anthra-sd, -1024, -1920-fse, -1920-fst,
-1920-ose, -1920-ost) install the sources and the conffile and run
vdr-skin-anthra-update in their postinst. Packages for Debian 13 are in
the trixie-main suite of https://apt.vdr-portal.de.

To change a skin, edit /etc/vdr/anthra/SKIN.conf, run

  vdr-skin-anthra-update SKIN

and restart VDR, see vdr-skin-anthra-update(8).

Building
--------

This is a native Debian package, build it with

  gbp buildpackage

or dpkg-buildpackage. The skins need text2skin with true colour mode
(>= 1.3.4+git20170702-4fnu0, e.g. 1.4.x from
https://github.com/unf/vdr-plugin-text2skin).
